{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-0710"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Iron Ore Mining Operations Coordinator"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "0710"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :mining/iron-ore
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:resource-stewardship :mine-safety :supply-resilience]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :iron-ore-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :telemetry]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "IronOps-LLM Advisor <-> Iron Ore Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph
 (langgraph.graph, ironops.operation/build), append-only audit ledger
 (ironops.store/ledger + append-ledger!, mem-store).
 Fixes a severe prior gap, present in BOTH the code AND this file's own
 sibling README: this repo previously had NO StateGraph at all --
 ironops.operation was just a static op-registry (a data map + two
 lookup functions, no graph, no wiring); the actual 'flow' lived as a
 hand-called chain inside ironops.sim's run-proposal function (advisor
 -> governor, nothing else -- a governor invoked directly from a demo
 file, never through any graph). ironops.ironopsllm had NO defprotocol
 Advisor at all -- just plain functions (mock-advisor/llm-advisor/
 advisor). NO ledger concept existed anywhere in ironops.store. And the
 README ACTIVELY made two false technical claims, not merely an
 overclaimed blueprint: its Architecture section claimed 'The
 governed-actor pattern (langgraph StateGraph + independent Governor
 ...)' when no StateGraph existed anywhere in the code, and its Store
 bullet claimed 'Protocol-based (MemStore for dev/test, DatomicStore
 for production)' when no DatomicStore ever existed at all. The
 README's own 'Tests' section additionally fabricated a count ('16
 tests / 35 assertions') against an actual 7 deftests (6 governor + 1
 store-contract). This blueprint nonetheless claimed
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented and listed :audit-ledger in
 :required-technologies, which was false given all of the above.
 Now: a genuinely compiled StateGraph (intake -> advise -> govern ->
 decide -+-> commit / request-approval -> commit / hold) with
 interrupt-before #{:request-approval} + an in-memory checkpointer for
 real human-in-the-loop resume; a real ironops.ironopsllm/Advisor
 protocol with MockAdvisor/LlmAdvisor records wrapping the SAME
 proposal-building logic that existed before (renamed mock-advisor/
 llm-advisor -> mock-proposal/llm-proposal, byte-identical bodies, to
 make room for the protocol's own mock-advisor/llm-advisor CONSTRUCTOR
 fns); and a real ironops.store/ledger + append-ledger! genuinely wired
 into the :commit/:hold graph nodes, not test-only. ironops.governor's
 five checks (forbidden-operation · no-spec-basis ·
 site-record-missing/not-verified · safety-concern-escalation ·
 confidence-floor) and ironops.phase's intake/verify/propose/resolved/
 hold transition table are reused UNCHANGED -- this fix only wires the
 existing mine-safety/coordination compliance policy into a real
 compiled graph and a real ledger, it does not redesign it. The
 governor's own verdict :hard?/:escalate? flags drive routing directly:
 :hard? true (checks 1-4, including safety-concern-escalation) is a
 PERMANENT block straight to :hold, never interactive; the ONLY
 interactive :request-approval path is check 5 (confidence floor)
 firing alone.
 Proven end-to-end by test/ironops/operation_test.clj (ledger stays
 empty until a real commit/hold, all five governor checks exercised
 through the REAL compiled graph including the safety-concern flag's
 permanent non-interactive hold, escalate-then-approve and
 escalate-then-reject for the sole low-confidence-only interactive
 path) plus a clojure -M:dev:run demo runner producing real ledger
 entries for every scenario -- 41 tests / 129 assertions in test/
 (up from 7 deftests before this fix), plus the pre-existing 1 test /
 5 assertions in test-cross-repo/ (ADR-2607999970's cross-actor
 pedigree export, unaffected by this fix). CI
 (.github/workflows/ci.yml) was missing entirely and is added in this
 fix. README.md's Architecture/Store/Tests sections and this file's
 own text are corrected to match, since the StateGraph/Governor/ledger
 claims are now genuinely true rather than being walked back."}
